Refuse to release a libfabric transfer handle that is still in flight.

NIXL 1.5.0's nixlLibfabricEngine::releaseReqH deletes the backend handle
unconditionally. Every request it posted captured that raw pointer in its
completion callback, so releasing a transfer before its completions land
leaves the progress thread calling complete_request() on freed memory.
NIXL 1.3.0 deleted nothing here, which is why the bump exposed this.

The core already handles a refusal. nixlAgent::releaseXferReq calls
releaseReqH on an IN_PROG request and, on a negative return, keeps the
request alive and reports NIXL_ERR_REPOST_ACTIVE to its caller. So return
that status and log at NIXL_WARN instead of freeing. A handle whose
requests have all completed still deletes, as it did before.

TODO(GEX-4324): propose this upstream and drop the patch once it lands.
The closest upstream work on the same lifetime problem is
ai-dynamo/nixl#2244.

diff --git a/src/plugins/libfabric/libfabric_backend.cpp b/src/plugins/libfabric/libfabric_backend.cpp
--- a/src/plugins/libfabric/libfabric_backend.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/libfabric/libfabric_backend.cpp
@@ -1704,7 +1704,19 @@
         return NIXL_SUCCESS;
     }
 
-    delete static_cast<nixlLibfabricBackendH *>(handle);
+    auto *backend_handle = static_cast<nixlLibfabricBackendH *>(handle);
+    if (!backend_handle->is_completed()) {
+        // Every posted request captures this pointer in its completion callback, so
+        // freeing it now leaves the progress thread writing to released memory. The
+        // core keeps the transfer alive when releaseReqH returns an error.
+        NIXL_WARN << "releaseReqH called with "
+                  << backend_handle->get_completed_requests_count() << " of "
+                  << backend_handle->get_submitted_requests_count()
+                  << " requests complete, refusing to free an in-flight transfer";
+        return NIXL_ERR_REPOST_ACTIVE;
+    }
+
+    delete backend_handle;
     NIXL_DEBUG << "releaseReqH completed successfully";
     return NIXL_SUCCESS;
 }
